course: dictionary
lesson: 6939
title: Pain: hurt, sadness, or a nuisance?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word pain can mean different things, so use the context to decide which one the writer means. «Pain is a warning sign, so take breaks and stop if it hurts.» Here pain is the feeling in your body that tells you something is wrong.
explain: «A doctor cannot feel your pain, so say clearly where it hurts, how it feels and when it started.» Only you can feel your pain, so this means the hurt you feel in your body.
explain: Pain can also mean great sadness, as in the pain of losing a pet. Be careful with «a pain», which is informal and means an annoying person or thing, as in «a pain in the neck». Always check the words around it.
explain: «Take pains» means try very hard to do something carefully. «No pain, no gain» means hard work brings good results.
fact: Pain is the feeling you have when part of your body is hurt or ill.
fact: Pain can also mean great sadness, as in the pain of losing a pet.
fact: «A pain» (informal) means an annoying person or thing.
fact: «Take pains» means try very hard to do something carefully.
fact: Pain is a warning signal from your nerves to your brain that something is wrong, so tell an adult about pain that is strong, keeps coming back, or follows a fall or bite.
exercise: «Pain is a warning sign, so take breaks and stop if it hurts.» What does pain mean here? | *The feeling you have when part of your body is hurt | A kind of sport | A happy song | A pair of tight shoes
exercise: Mia says, «He is such a pain in the neck!» What does a pain mean here? | *An annoying person | A very kind neighbour | A person who is very ill
exercise: Ruby felt the pain of losing her cat for weeks. What kind of pain is this? | Hunger | *Great sadness | Hurt in her leg | A sharp burn on her hand
test: «Chest pain or fainting during sport is never normal.» Why should you tell an adult about chest pain during sport? | *Because it is never normal | Because it means you are very strong | Because it shows you are winning | Because sport is boring
test: Sam will take pains to draw the map neatly. What does take pains mean? | Draw it in pain | Give up on the map | *Try very hard to do it carefully | Rush through it as fast as possible
exam: What does «no pain, no gain» mean? | Pain stops you from winning anything | Getting hurt is always good for you | Gain is a kind of pain | *Hard work brings good results
